hadiths[1]{hadithnumber,text}:
"1096","Chapter on the prohibition of burning living beings, 1135 - Bahr ibn Nasr al-Khawlani narrated to us, from Shu'ayb ibn al-Layth, from his father, from Bukayr, from Sulayman ibn Yasar, from Abu Hurayrah (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent us on an expedition and said: If you find so-and-so and so-and-so - two men of Quraysh - burn them both with fire. Then when we were about to set out the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I had ordered you to burn so-and-so and so-and-so with fire, yet none punishes with fire but Allah; so if you find them both, kill them both."
